# AngOS

**AngOS** is an independent operating system project for x86-64 computers.

The goal of AngOS is to create a complete, usable operating system by combining original AngOS code with carefully selected open-source components and projects created by other developers.

## Current Status

> 🚧 **Early development — not yet usable as a general-purpose operating system.**

AngOS is currently being built from the ground up. APIs, architecture, project structure, and other parts of the system are expected to change frequently.

## Goals

* x86-64 support
* UEFI and legacy BIOS boot support
* Custom AngOS kernel
* Custom AngOS boot protocol
* Modular architecture
* Open-source development
* Reuse of existing open-source software where appropriate
* Eventually provide a usable desktop and/or command-line operating environment

## Project Structure

```text
AngOS/
├── bootloader/     # AngOS boot system
├── kernel/         # AngOS kernel
├── userland/       # User-space programs
├── libraries/      # Shared libraries
├── tools/          # Development and build tools
├── docs/           # Documentation
└── third_party/    # Third-party components
```

## Third-Party Software

AngOS incorporates and/or may incorporate software created by other developers.

Third-party components retain their original copyrights and licenses. Their licenses are **not replaced by the AngOS license**.

Current third-party components will be documented in:

```text
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES
```

and, where appropriate, their original license files will be retained alongside the relevant source code.

## Licensing

Original AngOS source code is licensed separately from third-party components.

See [`LICENSE`](LICENSE) for the license covering original AngOS code.

See [`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES`](THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES) for third-party software, copyrights, licenses, and attribution requirements.

## Contributing

Contributions are welcome.

Before contributing code derived from another project, please make sure that its license permits the intended use and that all required copyright and license notices are preserved.

## Disclaimer

AngOS is experimental software under active development.

It may contain bugs, incomplete features, and breaking changes. Do not rely on AngOS for important data or production systems.
